-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the rigid H₁ classifying map at the Tate point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   **Valuation-theoretic data over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. $W$ is a finite set of places of the field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`) over that residue field, and the hypothesis `hW` says that a place belongs to $W$ exactly when it belongs to `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the set of places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`; $s$ is a chosen element of $W$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of the Laurent series field over $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$, the first being the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and the second the base change of the function field of the $H$-level curve of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ with upper field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` and residual field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring of the former together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the latter whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisor pushforward, and the compatibilities with $A$ recorded in the structure. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$.
--
--   **A small field of constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$. Write $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require that $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it be a Henselian local ring, and that its residue field be algebraically closed; `hκ` requires that every $a \in A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to (the image of) some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity and the level field.** $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity, and `hιξ` requires the existence of a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. $H_1$ is the subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ given by `hH₁` as the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; thus $H_1$ cuts out the level $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ inside level $q^2M'$. $K$ is an intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $k_0$, equal by `hK` to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the subfield generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of the rational $H_1$-level function field; $K$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure making $A_0 \to k_0 \to K$ a scalar tower. Finally $j$ is a nonzero element of $K$ whose image in the Laurent series field over $k_0$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb ↥k₀ ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81).
--
--   **Functoriality and rigidification data over $A_0$.** The hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL` assert, for all $A_0$-algebras $T$, that Weierstrass variable changes carry $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point data to $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point data (`IsGamma1Point` for the transformed datum `D.variableChange C`), carry `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` to `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k` for the transformed kernel polynomial `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`, and preserve divisibility of the polynomials `inLineMulPoly` in the corresponding transformed shape. $\mathcal G$ is a family of relative group laws (`GroupLaws A₀`) which is chord-tangent (`h𝒢`) and has the origin as identity in the origin chart (`h𝒢O`); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q` satisfying `IsSectionTransport` (`h𝒯`), i.e. its variable-change and base-change operations are compatible, up to the stated identifications of curves, with the graded homomorphisms on projective models and with the level sections $P$, $Q$. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` assert the existence, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ (respectively every $A_0$-algebra map $f : T \to T'$) and every projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, of a graded ring homomorphism between the projective-model graded rings satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom` (respectively `IsCoefficientHom`), together with the stated containment of irrelevant ideals.
--
--   **The moduli package and the Tate point.** $P_0$ is a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` over $A_0$ for the moduli datum `(rigidDataH1Pow ↥A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯).toLevelModuliDatum`, that is, an $A_0$-algebra $B_0 =$ `P₀.B₀` with a universal point such that every point over every $A_0$-algebra is induced by a unique $A_0$-algebra map out of $B_0$. $x_0$ is a $K$-point of this datum whose $j$-invariant `jOf x₀`, read in the Laurent series field over $k_0$, equals [`ModularCurve.jqNModC ↥k₀ q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (hypothesis `hx₀`). Further, `clC` is an $A_0$-algebra map from $B_0$ to the subalgebra [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥A₀ ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) of $K$, consisting of the elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$, and `hclC` says that composing `clC` with the inclusion into $K$ gives the classifying map `P₀.classify x₀`.
--
--   **The Tate description of $x_0$ (hypothesis `hμ`).** There exist a variable change $C$ over the Laurent series field over $k_0$ and a raw datum $r$ of the rigid data over $K$ such that: the class of $r$ is $x_0$; writing $t =$ `tateToricPoint ↥k₀ q (ξ^q)` for the toric point attached to the $q$-th power of the unit determined by $\xi$, one has $C.u \cdot (2t_1 + C(1/6)) = 2t_2 + t_1$ together with $C.r = C(-1/12)$, $C.s = C(-1/2)$, $C.t = C(1/24)$; the curve of $r$, pushed to the Laurent series field over $k_0$, equals $C \bullet$ `tateBase ↥k₀ q`; for every prime $p$ dividing $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the first level component `r.level.1 p`, pushed to the Laurent series field over $k_0$ and then coefficientwise along $f$, equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of the $f$-image of $C$ in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)` applied to $\prod_{1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2,\ p \nmid a} (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\ F'\, q\, \zeta^a)_1)$; the second level component `r.level.2.1`, pushed to the Laurent series field, equals the `LevelPData` $\langle t_1, t_2, t_1, t_2 \rangle$ transformed by $C$; and there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose images in the Laurent series field over $k_0$ are the four coordinates `xP`, `yP`, `xQ`, `yQ` of `(cuspData ↥k₀ q (ξ^{ℓ_g}) ![1,0] ![0,-1]).variableChange C`, such that `IsSectionThrough r.level.2.2.P Px Py` and `IsSectionThrough r.level.2.2.Q Qx Qy` hold.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $z \in K$ and every proof that $z$ lies in [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥A₀ ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), there exists $c \in B_0$ with `clC c` equal to $z$ viewed as an element of that subalgebra. Equivalently, the corestriction `clC` of the classifying map of the Tate point $x_0$ onto the algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$ is surjective.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the identification of the fine moduli ring of the rigid $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ moduli problem with the $j$-integral chart algebra of the level field $K$, in the shape used for the semistable model of the $H_1$-level modular curve at $q$ and computed at the Tate point. It is the input, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ setting, for producing preimages in $B_0$ of chart elements in the subsequent étale cyclic-quotient analysis.
